    "title": "What channel is the Men's Final Four on today? TV schedule, time for 2026 March Madness semifinal games | Sporting News",
    "text": "If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation. Learn more > The Men's Final Four will be pure cinema, taking place at Lucas Oil Stadium.Michigan, Arizona, Illinois and UConn are all taking a trip to Indianapolis for the national semifinals. The Huskies will look to grab another title after going back-to-back in 2023 and 2024. Arizona and Michigan are hoping to end long championship droughts, and Illinois is attempting to win the first title in program history. While two of these programs are No. 1 seeds, the others took down top dogs to secure their spots. UConn defeated No. 1 Duke with a shocking buzzer-beater, while Illinois beat Houston and an Iowa squad that pulled off an upset against defending champion Florida in the second round.Here is everything you need to know about the Men's Final Four, including TV and streaming options for the 2026 NCAA Tournament semifinals.What channel is the Men's Final Four on today?TV channel: TBS, truTVLive stream: DIRECTVBoth semifinal games and the national championship game will air on TBS and truTV. Fans can stream those games live on DIRECTV.Catch every game — try DIRECTV FREE today! Stream live MLB, March Madness, soccer and more with must-have sports channels like TNT, TBS, truTV, ESPN, FS1 and NFL Network — all included with DIRECTV.Start your FREE trial now and never miss a moment of the action. No contracts, no hassle, just wall-to-wall sports and entertainment. What time is the Men's Final Four today?Date: Saturday, April 4Time: 6:09 p.m. ET | 9:19 p.m. ETUConn vs. Illinois will tip off at 6:09 p.m. ET, and Michigan vs. Arizona will start at 9:19 p.m. ET on Saturday, April 4. Both games will be played at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.Men's Final Four schedule 2026Final FourSaturday, April 4GameTime (ET)TV/Live streamNo. 2 UConn 71, No. 3 Illinois 62——No. 1 Arizona vs. No. 1 Michigan9:19 p.m.TBS, truTV, DIRECTVNational championshipMonday, April 6GameTime (ET)TV/Live streamTBD vs. No. 2 UConn8:50 p.m.TBS, truTV, DIRECTVRelated Links2026 NCAA men's tournament bracketMen's college basketball scores, scheduleLatest men's college basketball newsHow to bet on college basketball",
